- op: discuss  # 1d6e
  at: '2026-06-29T00:55:10Z'  # 1d6e
  by: agent  # 1d6e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1d6e
  clock: 3  # 1d6e
  nonce: 1d6e  # 1d6e
  message: "Cluster design (2026-06-28, after WI-nurun completion; human greenlit the broad cross-cluster fix). Scope confirmed: INV-dadaf already SATISFIED (routes --input no longer writes artifacts). Open: INV-jumim (P1), WI-ribag (P2), WI-zipoj (P4), and this umbrella.\n\nRoot cause restated from the read-path map: generate_sketch (sketch.py) sources from repo_root filesystem walks — _analyze_test_files (find_files->rglob, the INV-jumim 60s bottleneck), the structure tree (rglob at ~1270/1350), _get_repo_languages, and config discovery — with NO precondition checking whether an authoritative source (the --input behavior map, or fresh cached analysis) already carries the data. Separately, centrality + per-file embeddings (WI-ribag) recompute on every warm sketch with no cache reuse.\n\nData partition (what the map authoritatively provides vs what genuinely needs disk):\n- FROM MAP (when --input given): the file/node universe, per-node is_test_file (test-file COUNT + paths), per-node language (language detection), per-node lines_of_code (LOC). The structure tree can be built from node paths.\n- NEEDS DISK (scoped to the map's files only): test-file framework-import detection + config/source CONTENT sections (the map stores no raw text). When --input is given these reads must be scoped to the map's file set, NOT a CWD rglob.\n\nDesign: a shared sketch read-path entry guard (SketchReadContext / cache-policy) that, when --input (or fresh cache) is present, derives universe/test-info/languages/structure from the map and restricts any residual disk reads to the map's files; plus a cache layer for centrality + per-file embeddings keyed like the analysis JSON.\n\nProposed staged PRs:\n- PR-A (INV-jumim, P1): map-driven test-file counting (short-circuit the rglob using is_test_file) + map-scoped universe/structure so --input summarizes the MAP, not a re-walked CWD. Fixes the 60s hang + the wrong-universe correctness bug (902-node pkg map -> whole-repo sketch).\n- PR-B (WI-ribag, P2): cache centrality + per-file embeddings so warm sketch reuses them (the 83s-run -> 202s-warm-sketch inversion).\n- PR-C (WI-zipoj, P4): validate at >1M-LOC scale + make comparison-sketch passes optional (WI-fufop's --no-comparison-sketches already exists; wire/default it).\n- INV-papuj closes when the shared read-path short-circuit + cache-policy is in place (the umbrella invariant)."  # 1d6e
- op: discuss  # 2640
  at: '2026-06-29T03:55:01Z'  # 2640
  by: agent  # 2640
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2640
  clock: 4  # 2640
  nonce: '2640'  # 2640
  message: "Cluster PR-A landed: INV-jumim satisfied via PR #320 (f6087587c3). The shared read-path seam is now in place — generate_sketch installs a synthetic FileIndex from the --input map's node paths so find_files/_analyze_test_files, languages, config, source-files, and the (now FileIndex-aware) Structure tree summarize the map's universe (no CWD re-walk). Remaining for the umbrella: PR-B (WI-ribag — cache centrality + per-file embeddings so a fully-warm sketch reuses them) and PR-C (WI-zipoj — >1M-LOC validation + default the comparison-sketch-optional path). INV-papuj closes once the centrality/embedding cache layer (the second half of the 'use-the-cache-when-available' precondition) lands."  # 2640
- op: discuss  # 2f27
